# react-native-enriched-markdown is an autolinked native module, so the
# whole package dir feeds the fingerprint runtime version. Two subtrees
# inside it are machine-local, not source: the grammar / tree-sitter /
# RaTeX assets its postinstall downloads (their pins live in
# grammar-versions.json and ratex-version.json, which stay hashed), and
# the per-app tree-sitter registry `pod install` codegens into
# cpp/highlight/vendor/generated-<app>/ (upstream #680). Hashing them made
# the fingerprint differ between a fresh checkout and a machine that had
# run pod install — EAS rejected the 0.2.1 build with a runtime version
# mismatch. Language set changes still bump the fingerprint through
# package.json.
